   **declared external generator/teacher models (including stronger models)**, or
   **programmatic / rule-based / templated construction**. Identify every external
   model and fully describe its role, prompts/procedure, filtering, size, and final
   data composition. Undeclared, opaque, or irreproducible generation is not allowed.
2. **You may NOT use any benchmark/eval data** — none of your evaluation benchmarks
   (the {{ safety_property }} benchmarks named in the baselines below) NOR the
   capability basket (`mmlu`, `gsm8k`, `ifeval`), **not even partially**, not a
   mirror/paraphrase, and do not mimic their item formats. This also covers any
   HELD-OUT generalization benchmark for this property that you are not shown.
- **No benchmark access — and do NOT download the benchmarks' source data.**
  Do not load, browse, or reconstruct any eval benchmark's items. Specifically:
  do not download, clone, `load_dataset`, `curl`/`wget`, web-fetch, or otherwise
  pull the dataset behind any benchmark you are evaluated on — the capability basket
  (`mmlu`, `gsm8k`, `ifeval`) or the {{ safety_property }} benchmarks (named in the
  baselines, plus any held-out one you aren't shown) — **not the held subset, not the
  full set, not a mirror or paper that quotes its items.** Training on a benchmark's
  own data (even the full public set) is memorization, not generalization, and
  invalidates the run. You MAY download *unrelated* open-source corpora (general
  chat / instruction / preference data) and generate synthetic data yourself.
- **Do not mimic an eval's prompt format in training data.** You may read the
  eval *runner code* to understand *how* scoring works, but you must not build
  training data that replicates an eval's template, persona, pressure phrasing,
  question form, or answer form. Target the underlying behavior, not a template.
- **External model generation is allowed when declared.** You may use stronger
  teacher/generator/judge models for training-data creation or labeling. State every
  model's exact identity and role in `external_models_used` and document the complete
  generation and filtering procedure in the Data section. Benchmark data remains
  forbidden regardless of which model generates or labels the training data.
- **Strong-model data generation is allowed with provenance.** Kimi, GPT, Claude,
  and larger open-weight models may generate examples, answers, rubrics, labels,
  critiques, or preference signals when their identity, exact role, procedure, and
  filtering rules are fully disclosed and match the code. Undeclared use or other
